                                <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white">How iOS Eye Tracking Works</h3>
                                <p class="text-zinc-400 text-[11px]">Apple Accessibility • Neural Engine & TrueDepth</p>
                                <p>Built directly into iOS and iPadOS, Eye Tracking gives users a hands-free way to navigate their iPhone using just their eyes. Powered by the front-facing camera and on-device machine learning, it calibrates in seconds without additional hardware.</p>
                                <div class="p-3 rounded-2xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
                                    <div class="font-semibold text-sky-300 mb-1">1. Dwell Control & Snap-to-Item</div>
                                    <p class="text-zinc-300">As your gaze moves across the screen, an on-screen pointer follows your focal point and magnetically snaps toward interactive buttons, reducing fatigue from micro-saccades.</p>
                                </div>
                                <div class="p-3 rounded-2xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
                                    <div class="font-semibold text-emerald-300 mb-1">2. Edge Auto-Scrolling</div>
                                    <p class="text-zinc-300">When reading long articles in Safari or browsing Settings, resting your gaze near the upper or lower edge smoothly scrolls content proportionally to your gaze depth.</p>
                                </div>
                                <div class="p-3 rounded-2xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
